IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa8-helpers`

-- coa8-part14-exemptions.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 14, ss 374 to 379: exemptions and supplementary provisions
-- (lines 4805-4844 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Several exemptions say only what something is NOT ("is not a political donation"): the decisive answer is then JUST FALSE
-- (the text says no) and every other case is NOTHING (the exemption does not reach it; section 364 or 365 decides).

§ `Exemptions`

-- ---- s 374: trade unions -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4810 | “trade union” has the meaning given by section 1 of Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (c. 52) or Article 3 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992 (S.I. 1992/807 (N.I. 5));
@ref s 374(3) "trade union" (src:4810)
GIVEN `has the meaning given by section 1 of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `has the meaning given by Article 3 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 374(3) the body is a trade union` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“trade union” has the meaning given by section 1 of Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a borrowed answer is not known
    `s 362 helper either answer`
        `has the meaning given by section 1 of the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992`
        `has the meaning given by Article 3 of the Industrial Relations (Northern Ireland) Order 1992`

-- src:4811 | “political fund” means the fund from which payments by a trade union in the furtherance of political objects are required to be made by virtue of section 82(1)(a) of that Act or Article 57(2)(a) of that Order.
@ref s 374(3) "political fund" (src:4811)
GIVEN `is the fund from which payments by a trade union in the furtherance of political objects are required to be made by virtue of section 82(1)(a) of that Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `is the fund from which payments by a trade union in the furtherance of political objects are required to be made by virtue of Article 57(2)(a) of that Order` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 374(3) the fund is a political fund` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“political fund” means the fund from which payments by a trade union in the furtherance of political objects are required to be made"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where a borrowed answer is not known
    `s 362 helper either answer`
        `is the fund from which payments by a trade union in the furtherance of political objects are required to be made by virtue of section 82(1)(a) of that Act`
        `is the fund from which payments by a trade union in the furtherance of political objects are required to be made by virtue of Article 57(2)(a) of that Order`

-- src:4807 | (1) A donation to a trade union, other than a contribution to the union's political fund, is not a political donation for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 374(1) A donation to a trade union is not a political donation (src:4807)
GIVEN `s 374(3) the payee is a trade union` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 374(3) the donation is a contribution to the union's political fund` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 374(1) the donation to the trade union is a political donation for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    IF `s 362 helper both answers` `s 374(3) the payee is a trade union` (`s 362 helper the opposite answer` `s 374(3) the donation is a contribution to the union's political fund`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A donation to a trade union, other than a contribution to the union's political fund, is not a political donation for the purposes of this Part"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption reaches only a donation to a trade union that is not a contribution to its political fund; section 364 decides the rest

-- src:4808 | (2) A trade union is not a political organisation for the purposes of section 365 (meaning of “political expenditure”).
@ref s 374(2) A trade union is not a political organisation for the purposes of section 365 (src:4808)
GIVEN `s 374(3) the body is a trade union` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 374(2) the trade union is a political organisation for the purposes of section 365` MEANS
    IF `s 374(3) the body is a trade union` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A trade union is not a political organisation for the purposes of section 365"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption names only a trade union

-- ---- s 375: subscription for membership of trade association -----------------------------------------------------

-- src:4815 | “trade association” means an organisation formed for the purpose of furthering the trade interests of its members, or of persons represented by its members, and
@ref s 375(2) "trade association" (src:4815)
GIVEN `formed for the purpose of furthering the trade interests of its members, or of persons represented by its members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375(2) the organisation is a trade association` MEANS
    IF `formed for the purpose of furthering the trade interests of its members, or of persons represented by its members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“trade association” means an organisation formed for the purpose of furthering the trade interests of its members"

-- src:4816 | “subscription” does not include a payment to the association to the extent that it is made for the purpose of financing any particular activity of the association.
@ref s 375(2) "subscription" (src:4816)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it made for the purpose of financing any particular activity of the association` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 375(2) the part of the payment that is a subscription` MEANS
    max 0 (`the payment` MINUS `the part of it made for the purpose of financing any particular activity of the association`)

-- src:4813 | (1) A subscription paid to a trade association for membership of the association is not a political donation for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 375(1) A subscription to a trade association is not a political donation (src:4813)
GIVEN `s 375(2) the organisation is a trade association` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the sum is a subscription paid for membership of the association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375(1) the subscription is a political donation for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    IF `s 375(2) the organisation is a trade association` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the sum is a subscription paid for membership of the association`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A subscription paid to a trade association for membership of the association is not a political donation for the purposes of this Part"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption reaches only a subscription paid to a trade association for membership; section 364 decides the rest

-- ---- s 376: all-party parliamentary groups -----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4819 | (2) An “all-party parliamentary group” means an all-party group composed of members of one or both of the Houses of Parliament (or of such members and other persons).
@ref s 376(2) "all-party parliamentary group" (src:4819)
GIVEN `an all-party group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `composed of members of one or both of the Houses of Parliament (or of such members and other persons)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376(2) the group is an all-party parliamentary group` MEANS
    IF `an all-party group` AND `composed of members of one or both of the Houses of Parliament (or of such members and other persons)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An “all-party parliamentary group” means an all-party group composed of members of one or both of the Houses of Parliament"

-- src:4818 | (1) An all-party parliamentary group is not a political organisation for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 376(1) An all-party parliamentary group is not a political organisation (src:4818)
GIVEN `s 376(2) the group is an all-party parliamentary group` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 376(1) the group is a political organisation for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    IF `s 376(2) the group is an all-party parliamentary group` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An all-party parliamentary group is not a political organisation for the purposes of this Part"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exemption names only an all-party parliamentary group

-- ---- s 377: political expenditure exempted by order ------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 377(2) (what an order may cover) and s 377(4) (affirmative resolution procedure) are order-making machinery: inert, reason 2 (fork F2).
-- Whether an order exempts the expenditure is a fact about an order that is not among the sources: an input.

-- src:4821 | (1) Authorisation under this Part is not needed for political expenditure that is exempt by virtue of an order of the Secretary of State under this section.
@ref s 377(1) Authorisation not needed for expenditure exempt by order (src:4821)
GIVEN `the expenditure is exempt by virtue of an order of the Secretary of State under this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 377(1) authorisation under this Part is not needed for the political expenditure` MEANS
    IF `the expenditure is exempt by virtue of an order of the Secretary of State under this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the orders made under this section are not among the sources

-- src:4826 | (3) If or to the extent that expenditure is exempt from the requirement of authorisation under this Part by virtue of an order under this section, it shall be disregarded in determining what donations are authorised by any resolution of the company passed for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 377(3) Exempt expenditure is disregarded in determining what a resolution authorises (src:4826)
GIVEN `the political expenditure` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is exempt by virtue of an order under this section` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 377(3) the amount of the expenditure counted in determining what a resolution authorises` MEANS
    max 0 (`the political expenditure` MINUS `the part of it that is exempt by virtue of an order under this section`)

-- ---- s 378: donations not amounting to more than £5,000 in any twelve month period ----------------------------------------

-- src:4832 | exceeds £5,000.
@ref s 378(1) The £5,000 limit (src:4832)
`s 378(1) the limit on donations in twelve months, in pounds` MEANS 5000

-- src:4834 | “donation” means a donation to a political party or other political organisation or to an independent election candidate; and
@ref s 378(2) "donation" (src:4834)
GIVEN `to a political party or other political organisation or to an independent election candidate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(2) the payment is a donation for the purposes of this section` MEANS
    IF `to a political party or other political organisation or to an independent election candidate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“donation” means a donation to a political party or other political organisation or to an independent election candidate"

DECLARE `s 378(2) relation of the other donor to the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 378(2) the company itself`
    `s 378(2) a subsidiary of the company`
    `s 378(2) a holding company of the company`
    `s 378(2) another subsidiary of a holding company of the company`
    `s 378(2) none of those`

-- src:4835 | “other relevant donations” means—
-- src:4836 | (a) in relation to a donation made by a company that is not a subsidiary, any other donations made by that company or by any of its subsidiaries;
-- src:4837 | (b) in relation to a donation made by a company that is a subsidiary, any other donations made by that company, by any holding company of that company or by any other subsidiary of any such holding company.
@ref s 378(2) "other relevant donations" (src:4835-4837)
-- (a) a company that is not a subsidiary: other donations by that company or by any of its subsidiaries;
-- (b) a subsidiary: other donations by that company, by any holding company of it, or by any other subsidiary of any such holding company.
-- A subsidiary of the company is read as a subsidiary of its holding company, so it counts under (b) as well (fork F4).
GIVEN `s 1159(1) the company making this donation is a subsidiary of another company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      relation IS A `s 378(2) relation of the other donor to the company`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(2) the other donation is an other relevant donation` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“other relevant donations” means"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) where the company's status as a subsidiary (section 1159) is not known and the donor's relation depends on it
    CONSIDER relation
    WHEN `s 378(2) the company itself` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 378(2) a subsidiary of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 378(2) none of those` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `s 1159(1) the company making this donation is a subsidiary of another company`
        WHEN JUST sub THEN JUST sub
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- src:4831 | (b) other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date on which that donation is made,
@ref s 378(1)(b) The twelve months ending with the date of the donation (src:4831)
-- "the period of 12 months ending with the date on which that donation is made": it begins the day after the same date a year earlier
-- (`add years` clamps 29 February to 28 February, so the window for 29 February 2024 begins on 1 March 2023).
GIVEN `the date of the other donation` IS A DATE
      `the date of this donation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(1)(b) the other donation falls in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation` MEANS
    IF `the date of the other donation` AT MOST `the date of this donation` AND `the date of the other donation` AT LEAST `add years` `the date of this donation` (-1) PLUS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date on which that donation is made"

-- src:4829 | (1) Authorisation under this Part is not needed for a donation except to the extent that the total amount of—
-- src:4830 | (a) that donation, and
-- src:4831 | (b) other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date on which that donation is made,
-- src:4832 | exceeds £5,000.
@ref s 378(1) Authorisation not needed except to the extent the total exceeds £5,000 (src:4829-4832)
GIVEN `this donation` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 378(1) the part of this donation for which authorisation is needed` MEANS
    min `this donation` (max 0 (`this donation` PLUS `the total of the other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation` MINUS `s 378(1) the limit on donations in twelve months, in pounds`))

-- src:4829 | (1) Authorisation under this Part is not needed for a donation except to the extent that the total amount of—
-- src:4830 | (a) that donation, and
-- src:4831 | (b) other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date on which that donation is made,
-- src:4832 | exceeds £5,000.
@ref s 378(1) Authorisation not needed except to the extent the total exceeds £5,000 (src:4829-4832)
GIVEN `this donation` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 378(1) authorisation is not needed for the whole of this donation` MEANS
    IF `this donation` PLUS `the total of the other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation` AT MOST `s 378(1) the limit on donations in twelve months, in pounds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except to the extent that the total amount of ... exceeds £5,000"

-- src:4838 | (3) If or to the extent that a donation is exempt by virtue of this section from the requirement of authorisation under this Part, it shall be disregarded in determining what donations are authorised by any resolution passed for the purposes of this Part.
@ref s 378(3) An exempt donation is disregarded in determining what a resolution authorises (src:4838)
GIVEN `this donation` IS A NUMBER
      `the total of the other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 378(3) the amount of this donation counted in determining what a resolution authorises` MEANS
    `s 378(1) the part of this donation for which authorisation is needed` `this donation` `the total of the other relevant donations made in the period of 12 months ending with the date of this donation`

-- ---- s 379: minor definitions -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4842 | “director” includes shadow director; and
@ref s 379(1) "director" includes shadow director (src:4842)
GIVEN `s 250 the person occupies the position of director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 251 the person is a shadow director` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379(1) the person is a director for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    IF `s 362 helper either answer` `s 250 the person occupies the position of director` `s 251 the person is a shadow director` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“director” includes shadow director"

-- src:4843 | “organisation” includes any body corporate or unincorporated association and any combination of persons.
@ref s 379(1) "organisation" includes bodies corporate, unincorporated associations and combinations of persons (src:4843)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person`
      `the persons form a combination of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379(1) the body is an organisation for the purposes of this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a company registered under the Companies Act 2006` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a body corporate incorporated outside the United Kingdom` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an unincorporated association` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the persons form a combination of persons`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“organisation” includes any body corporate or unincorporated association and any combination of persons"

-- src:4844 | (2) Except as otherwise provided, any reference in this Part to the time at which a donation is made or expenditure is incurred is, in a case where the donation is made or expenditure incurred in pursuance of a contract, any earlier time at which that contract is entered into by the company.
@ref s 379(2) The time at which a donation is made or expenditure is incurred (src:4844)
-- "any earlier time at which that contract is entered into by the company" (except as otherwise provided: see s 369(5)).
GIVEN `the date on which the donation is made or the expenditure is incurred` IS A DATE
      `it is made or incurred in pursuance of a contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which that contract is entered into by the company` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 379(2) the time at which the donation is made or the expenditure is incurred` MEANS
    IF `it is made or incurred in pursuance of a contract` AND `the date on which that contract is entered into by the company` LESS THAN `the date on which the donation is made or the expenditure is incurred`
    THEN `the date on which that contract is entered into by the company`
    ELSE `the date on which the donation is made or the expenditure is incurred`
